Z||000006||Monkeyman||05-28-2000||10:43 PM||||Cooter--Nice ride.  Love the T-tops!  Just a couple of suggestions (since you didn't ask).  First, get a wing.  Second, get rid of the "Why-don't-I-do-some-free-advertising-for-the-car-dealer" sticker on the bumper.  Also, if you're going with the monochromatic look (which I happen to like), why don't you paint the moldings?  Maybe in a slightly lighter shade of maroon?  If you're gonna stick with the stock wheels, are you planning on repainting them, too?  Maybe the same lighter shade of maroon I just talked you into for the molding? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||05-28-2000||11:15 PM||||I have never been much on keeping a car original, until now. The GT did not come with a wing, so a wing it will not have. The dealer sticker on the rear bumper is from when the car was bought new. All this car is going to get is a comfy place in my garage and some TLC. The keys even still have the "knock out" with the key number on them and they are on the dealer logo key ring. Both previous owners were women, the second one kept the car garaged and serviced every 2500 miles. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||sluppy123||05-28-2000||11:37 PM||||Cooter-<B>Good call on the wing</B>. People always tell me I should put a wing on my GT', But I think they look cleaner with no wing, plus it was born with no wing so it's going to live with no wing.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||05-29-2000||01:28 AM||||FLAT DECKS RULE!!!  <BR>I personally can't figure out why, with so much "ricer" bashing going on in this forum, how any one coud suggest adding a big, heavy, useless blind spot to a car that serves no purpose other then to screw up the lines of the car. Why not put an H on the nose while yer at it!<BR>LET THE FLAMES BEGIN!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||05-29-2000||02:16 AM||||Gentleman--To each his/her own.  Personally I like wings.  (Of course, I prefer notchbacks, too.)<P>Cooter--I didn't know about the originality of the car.  Just giving my .17 cents worth (inflation <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">).  If that car is going to be/stay exactly as it came from the dealer, then I'd say you're doing the right thing.  How many miles are on the car?||||reg||1
Z||000011||stimpy||05-29-2000||05:36 PM||||I have to admit, I think the wing is far more appropriate on the notch then the GT. The lines of the GT are so crisp in that 3/4 rear view w/o the wing. I'm not putting down cars that are equipped with one, but to spend the $$$ that I have heard being charged for a wing, drill holes in a good flat deck ( which from what I can tell, aren't that common) well, it jut seems heretical to me.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||05-29-2000||07:02 PM||||MM- my other 88 gt- the red one- has the wing. I like the looks of it, but just dont want to add it to the T-top car. BTW it has 100,000 miles on it. A little too many, but my other one has 180,000 on it.||||reg||1
